{
  "_comment": "Rotation state for the code-review sweep. A slice is one plugin (a folder name shared across the app/api, components, lib and mobile layers, plus the page folder of that name under app/ or app/apps/, reviewed together), one standalone module (a folder name in just one layer), or one catch-all (web-pages, web-shell, mobile-shell, <name>-package, scripts, ops, sql, ctf-root) holding every source file no named slice claims. Each run reviews an in-progress slice first, then one with findings left over from a capped run (`deferred`), then any never-reviewed slice, then the least-recently-reviewed one. `partial`, `nextFile` and `nextOffset` carry a too-big slice across runs so nothing is dropped; `updatedAt` moves on every write to a row. New slices start unreviewed (lastReviewedAt: null); slices whose folders are gone are pruned. This copy on main is stamped by the hand route (/rs, via `--stamp`); the scheduled sweep keeps its own copy on the code-review-ledger branch and merges this one on every run, the row written most recently winning per slice. Maintained by ctf/scripts/reviewCodebaseSlice.mjs; use its --pick, --stamp and --reconcile modes rather than editing by hand.",
